# Mapping of a torch.fx symbolic_trace graph (torch 2.13):
#   forward(x, bias): return relu(matmul(x, w) + bias)
#
# Placeholders become arguments, FX node names become value names, and callable
# targets become attributes. FX tensors carry no static types, so none are
# written: the checker stays out of the way (gradual typing) until a pass or an
# agent adds them.
func @mlp(%x, %bias) {
  %w = fx.get_attr target="w"
  %mm = fx.call_function %x, %w target="torch.matmul"
  %sum = fx.call_function %mm, %bias target="operator.add"
  %act = fx.call_function %sum target="torch.relu"
  return %act
}
